# Code Readability Rules

## Naming

- Use full, explicit names, no abbreviations (`userCount`, not `usrCnt`)
- Name functions as action verbs (`calculateTotal`, `isValid`)
- Prefix booleans with `is`, `has`, `can`, `should`

## Functions

- One function = one responsibility
- Max ~20-30 lines per function
- Max 3 parameters, otherwise use an object
- Prefer early returns over nested conditionals

## Structure

- No more than 2-3 levels of indentation
- Extract complex conditions into named variables/functions
- Group related code, separate unrelated blocks with blank lines

## Magic values

- No hardcoded values (numbers or strings): always use named constants
- Centralize configuration, don't scatter it across the code

## Comments

- Comment the "why", never the "what"
- Remove dead or commented-out code, don't keep it "just in case"

## Simplicity

- No over-engineering (YAGNI)
- Prefer simple, readable solutions over "clever" ones
- No abstraction until there's a real, proven need

## Errors

- Never leave an empty catch/except block
- Error messages should be explicit and actionable

## Consistency

- Follow the existing style of the project
- Let the formatter/linter decide, never debate style manually
